    "body": "_Requested by **Sia** · stage 2 of #498_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` after #506 (and #505); no other open PR is needed first.\n- Touches `sp-bibprocess`, `sp-litnotes-titles`, `-refs` and `-meta`, `sp-notes`, `sp-vulpea-convert-properties` (each with its doc and tests) and the view doc.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-4a39fy`: the cloud proxy cannot rename a branch, so it needs the number prefix from Sia.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The BibTeX lint report is sections of items: the fixes are an action section (RET runs one), then the entries with problems, then a section per kind (files, crossref, date, keys, duplicates, surnames, merge).\n- The crossref dry run, litnote titles, litnote references, meta fill-all, notes filing and the property preview are sections of items too.\n- Counts and flags are items with `:key nil`, so `d` only drops real entries.\n- Notes filing cuts its plan at apply time (the dashboard drops in place, so no redraw runs).\n- The view doc lists which reports use it.\n- Dropping a row does not change the counts on the Fix buttons until `g`.\n\n## Tests (batch Emacs 29.3, container)\n\n- `sp-bibprocess-lint`: 104 of 106 pass; the 2 failures (`indent`, `dup-test-choose-value`) fail the same way before this PR (Org/`goggles` missing).\n- `sp-litnotes-refs`, `sp-vulpea-convert-properties`, `sp-bibtex-zotero`, `sp-batch-report-view`: all pass.\n- `sp-litnotes-titles`, `sp-notes`, `sp-litnotes-meta`, `sp-vulpea-meta-order`: no failure that was not there before; the rest fail before and after for the Org reason. These need a run on the Mac.\n- Tests that read Org text bind `sp-batch-report-display` to `org`; new tests check the sections.\n- Not measured: the GUI, and the speed of these reports with a real vault.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun`: the Fix items run their fix on RET; `d`/`u` drop and restore an entry; `A` applies\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun` and `sp-litnotes-refs-dryrun`: sections, links open the note, `d` drops a note, `A` leaves it out\n- [ ] `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill-all-dryrun`: counts, to-change notes with their lines, skipped sections\n- [ ] `M-x sp-notes-filing-dryrun`: moves list; drop one file and apply: it stays where it is\n- [ ] `M-x sia-vulpea-convert-all-notes-properties-to-meta-dryrun`: preview, drop, apply\n- [ ] Set `sp-batch-report-display` to `org`: the same reports still open as Org\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9bi8g2P4sdH8GttsS)_",
